      "Baptist missionaries J. Edgar and Mary Davis founded the Baptist Spanish Publishing House in Toluca, Mexico, where on 17 November 1905 Davis printed his first Spanish book on a foot-powered press in his kitchen. During the Mexican Revolution the press left Mexico and settled in El Paso in 1916. Since 1938 it has stood on the site of the former Baptist tuberculosis sanatorium. Now known as Editorial Mundo Hispano, it closed its presses in 2000 and in 2005 was described as the world's oldest evangelical Spanish publishing house.",
