      "A. B. Simpson founds the Missionary Training Institute in New York City in 1882, with a formal program in place by 1883, to train workers for the world's \"neglected peoples\". The school bought land at South Nyack, about 30 miles up the Hudson, and moved there. It later became Nyack Missionary College in 1956, Nyack College in 1972 and Alliance University, and Wikipedia lists the institution as active from 1882 to 2023. Its roots tie it to the Christian and Missionary Alliance Simpson founded.",
