      "On 11 June 1936, in Philadelphia, ministers and elders who had left the Presbyterian Church in the U.S.A. form the denomination first called the Presbyterian Church of America, with J. Gresham Machen as first moderator. Machen had founded an Independent Board for Presbyterian Foreign Missions in 1933, and after he and seven other clergy refused to disavow it they were suspended. In 1939, after the older church sued over the name, the body took the name Orthodox Presbyterian Church. Machen died on 1 January 1937.",
